.TH TOHA3EE 1 "August 2026" "toha3ee 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
toha3ee \- network exploitation and MITM framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B toha3ee
[\fIflags\fR]
.br
.B toha3ee
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B toha3ee
is an interactive network security console: it discovers hosts, enumerates
services, profiles attack surfaces and carries out authorised MITM, wireless
and credential-based testing from a single REPL. It ships 73 modules across
the recon, scan, enumeration, OSINT, authentication, MITM, wireless, switch
and post-exploitation categories, plus a scripting engine for repeatable
engagements.

.B toha3ee
is an authorised-security tool. Use it only on systems and networks you own
or have explicit written permission to test. See
.BR security (1)
for responsible-use guidance.

Most modules need raw-socket, capture or IP-forwarding privileges. The console
escalates to root via
.BR sudo (8)
automatically; pass
.B \-\-no\-sudo
to run unprivileged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Config file path (default \fItoha3ee.json\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-eval " commands"
Run a one-shot command sequence and exit, e.g.
.RS
toha3ee \-\-eval "net.scan; net.show"
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-events " spec"
Emit a machine-readable JSONL event stream alongside the run:
.BR stdout ,
.BR stderr ,
or a file path, which is created/truncated with mode 0600.
Each line is a self-describing event carrying schema_version, timestamp,
execution_id, framework, level, event and data; it is the canonical feed for
agents and CI. Omit or pass an empty string to disable the stream.
.TP
.BI \-\-iface " iface"
Network interface to attack from.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable coloured output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sudo
Do not auto-escalate to root via sudo.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " format"
Output format for the
.B report
and
.B version
commands: \fIterminal\fR (default), \fIjson\fR, or \fImarkdown\fR.
Machine-readable output never leaks plaintext credentials; only the JSON
session report file does, and it is written 0600.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Verbose logging.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help for toha3ee or a subcommand.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Validate a
.I .toha3ee
script and print a dry-run plan without sending packets.
.TP
.B eval
Run a one-shot command sequence and exit (same as the
.B \-\-eval
flag).
.TP
.B interactive, repl, shell
Start the interactive console (the default action when no command is given).
.TP
.B modules
List all registered modules with their risk level and description.
.TP
.B report
Render a saved session report (default
.IR toha3ee-report.json )
in the format given by
.BR \-o .
.TP
.B run
Execute a script or caplet non-interactively.
.TP
.B script
Execute a
.I .toha3ee
script file.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and banner (honours
.BR \-o " json" ).
.TP
.B wizard
Guided attack setup: step through target, interface and module choices.
.TP
.B completion
Generate the shell autocompletion script for the specified shell.
.TP
.B help
Show help about any command.
.SH THE CONSOLE
Interactive mode drops you into a REPL with a status HUD that live-counts
live hosts, ports, credentials and events.
.SS Core commands
.TP
.B on <module>
Start a module, e.g.
.BR "on net.scan" .
.TP
.B off <module>
Stop a running module.
.TP
.B stop <module>
Alias of
.BR off .
.TP
.B net.show
List discovered hosts (IP, MAC, vendor, OS guess).
.TP
.B net.profile
Ranked attack vectors for the target set.
.TP
.B exec -> <module>
Run a one-shot module, e.g.
.BR "exec -> report.generate" .
.TP
.B set <key> <value>
Set a config key.
.TP
.B get <key>
Read a config key.
.TP
.B modules
Print the module catalogue.
.TP
.B help
Show console help.
.TP
.B quit
Exit the console.
.SS Scripting
Scripts are
.I .toha3ee
files: one command per line with conditionals, variables, iteration and
module control. Validate without executing:
.RS
toha3ee build scripts/full-pipeline.toha3ee
.RE
Run for real:
.RS
sudo toha3ee script scripts/full-pipeline.toha3ee
.RE
See
.BR scripting (7)
for the language reference.
.SH MODULES
The 73 modules are grouped into categories. The main ones:
.TP
.B recon
net.ping, net.scan, net.ip6sweep, net.traceroute, net.osdetect, osint.* (asn,
bucket, ct, dns, dork, github, harvest, hibp, metadata, shodan, wayback,
whois), cve.suggest.
.TP
.B scan
service.synscan, service.tcpconnect, service.ack, service.finxmas,
service.idle, service.protoscan, service.udpscan, service.fingerprint,
service.tls, web.dir, web.misconfig, pcap.export.
.TP
.B enum
snmp.enum, ldap.enum, smb.enum, nfs.enum, smtp.enum, dns.rebind.
.TP
.B auth
default.creds, smb.signing, smb.kerberoast, ntlm.relay, auth.brute,
auth.spray, auth.asrep, auth.userenum.
.TP
.B mitm
arp.spoof, dhcp.starve, dhcp.rogue, dns.spoof, http.harvest, http.proxy,
https.proxy, ssl.strip, icmp.redirect, llmnr.poison, wpad.poison,
dhcp6.spoof, ipv6.ra, ipv6.ndp.
.TP
.B wireless
wlan.scan, wlan.deauth, wlan.handshake, wlan.pmkid, wlan.beaconflood,
wlan.karma, wlan.eviltwin.
.TP
.B switch
switch.flood, switch.portsteal, switch.vlanhop, switch.cdp, switch.stp.
.TP
.B espionage
phish.inject, session.replay.
.TP
.B post
report.generate.
.PP
Run
.B "toha3ee modules"
for the complete, current list with risk levels.
.SH CONFIGURATION
toha3ee reads
.I toha3ee.json
from the current directory (override with
.BR \-\-config ).
Keys are grouped by module, for example:
.RS
toha3ee> set arp.spoof.targets 10.0.0.5,10.0.0.6
.br
toha3ee> set wlan.deauth.bssid 00:11:22:33:44:55
.br
toha3ee> set phish.inject.brand microsoft
.RE
Environment variables override config for the same keys:
.B TOHA3EE_NO_SUDO=1
disables auto-escalation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I toha3ee.json
Configuration file.
.TP
.I toha3ee-report.md
Report written by the
.B report.generate
module.
.TP
.I scripts/
Bundled
.I .toha3ee
scripts, including
.I full-pipeline.toha3ee
.
.TP
.I man/toha3ee.1
This manual page.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TOHA3EE_NO_SUDO
When set to a non-empty value, disables auto-escalation (same as
.BR \-\-no\-sudo ).
.TP
.B TOHA3EE_VERSION, TOHA3EE_PREFIX, TOHA3EE_SKIP_PATH
Installer options, see
.BR install.sh .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error, failed preflight, or script failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT/SIGTERM (after automatic cleanup).
.SH SECURITY
This tool is capable of disrupting networks. It must only be used with
authorisation. Modules are subject to preflight checks, a safety manager
(heartbeat watchdog, automatic cleanup) and a risk classifier; the
.B net.profile
command surfaces ranked vectors before anything is run. Review
.BR security (7)
before your first real engagement.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scripting (7),
.BR security (7),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR tcpdump (8)
.PP
Full documentation lives in the repository's
.I docs/
tree: getting-started, user-guide, module-reference, configuration, scripting,
architecture, reporting, faq and security.
.SH AUTHOR
The toha3ee project. Report issues at
https://github.com/qyvora/qyvora-toha3ee/issues.
